',
  '<p class="gd-p">Your training path is under <b class="gd-ui">Me</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Academy</b>. There is a path for each of your functions: customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person or remote, field work.</p><section class="gd-task" id="academy-watch-the-lessons" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Watch the lessons</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Academy</b>. Each path lists its sections in order, with Passed, Open or Pass the one before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open a section. Each lesson is a short video made by your browser: scenes with captions, read aloud by your browser&#39;s own voice.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Play</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Pause</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Back</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Next</b> move through the scenes; <b class="gd-ui">Replay</b> starts again; Speed goes from 0.75x to 1.5x. <b class="gd-ui">Voice on</b> turns the voice off and on.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">No sound or no English voice on your device? The lesson plays with captions only, each scene timed for reading.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Use headphones in the office. The voice is your browser&#39;s, so it can sound different on another device.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-pass-the-quiz" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pass the quiz</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Under the lessons, answer every question and press <b class="gd-ui">Check my answers</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">You need 80% (the pass mark in Program settings). Passed: the next section opens. Not yet: each answer shows the right one and why; press <b class="gd-ui">Try again</b> as often as you need.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A section that is on two of your paths (the policies, for example) counts on both once passed.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>An Admin can open a section early for you, for example when you already did this work somewhere else. The academy gate is on: each section opens once you pass the one before it. If you were hired with one-step Hire, the rest of the portal waits until you pass your paths (the guide and your profile stay open). Each path ends with a section on what changed recently.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-your-first-steps-welcome-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your first steps: Welcome (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your first sign-in opens <b class="gd-ui">Welcome</b>, your onboarding checklist, in four steps:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Welcome.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Your profile and phone: add your home address and your mobile number in your profile.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The academy: pass every section of your path. Each quiz passes at 80%, and you can retake it as often as you need.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Your first tasks: press <b class="gd-ui">Done</b> on each one as you finish it.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Until you pass the academy, Welcome, the academy, the guide and your profile are all that opens; any other page brings you back to Welcome. Then <b class="gd-ui">Go to your portal</b> opens everything.</p></section>');
-- GUIDES 0826 END

-- ================================================================ the grants of part P's functions
-- 0821 to 0825 revoked them from public, anon and authenticated but never granted service_role (the server), so the
-- server could not run them. Every app function made by part P gets the usual pair.
do $$
declare f record;
begin
  for f in select p.oid::regprocedure as sig from pg_proc p join pg_namespace n on n.oid = p.pronamespace
            where n.nspname = 'app' and p.proname = any (array[
              'documents_onboarding_review', 'government_form_fill_read', 'government_forms_can', 'government_forms_list', 'government_forms_make_again',
              'onboarding_overview', 'onboarding_owners', 'onboarding_photo_file', 'onboarding_photo_get', 'onboarding_photo_kind', 'onboarding_photo_label',
              'onboarding_photo_remove', 'onboarding_photo_replace', 'onboarding_photo_review', 'onboarding_photo_unapprove', 'onboarding_photo_who',
              'onboarding_photos', 'owner_add_vins', 'owner_terms_retire', 'vehicles_owner_terms_retire', 'registry_forms_after', 'registry_forms_due',
              'registry_forms_on_change', 'registry_forms_refresh'])
  loop
    execute format('revoke all on function %s from public, anon, authenticated', f.sig);
    execute format('grant execute on function %s to service_role', f.sig);
  end loop;
end $$;
